@startuml
title Scheduled Live Refresh and Historical Backfill
start
:Run the five-minute parking scheduler;
if (facility catalog refresh due?) then (yes)
  :Call /carpark without facility;
  :Cache facility IDs and names;
endif
:For each enabled facility, sequentially call /carpark?facility={facilityId};
:Map MessageDate from Sydney local time to UTC Instant;
:Upsert newest sample into the matching ten-minute bucket;
note right: Every enabled facility is attempted once per five-minute round.
if (every fifth scheduler run?) then (yes)
  :Select facility and provider eventdate request;
  :Call /carpark/history?facility={facilityId}&eventdate={date};
  :Map and upsert records by their actual Sydney dates;
  :Complete the history request work item on success;
endif
if (provider request failed?) then (yes)
  :Set historical work to RETRY_WAIT when applicable;
  :Record retryAfter;
else (no)
  :Keep processing later scheduled slots;
endif
:Return;
stop

note right
  /carpark?facility=... supplies the latest occupancy record for live refresh.
  /carpark without facility supplies the catalog.
  /carpark/history is only for historical retrieval.

  MessageDate is Sydney local time without an offset. Convert it using
  Australia/Sydney and store the resulting Instant in UTC. Ignore the legacy
  `time` field. Group all records by the Sydney date from MessageDate, not by
  the requested eventdate.

  Treat eventdate as an untrusted request parameter, not a storage date.
  Persist every returned sample according to its Sydney-local MessageDate,
  even when that falls before or after the requested eventdate. A successful
  live response never completes historical request work. History completion
  records that the requested history operation succeeded; it does not claim
  complete sample coverage for that Sydney date.

  Provider calls run sequentially. A live refresh round includes one call per
  enabled facility; a history request is attempted every fifth round. Catalog
  refreshes are additional calls every six hours. Retry failed history
  requests later through the scheduler; bucket upserts are idempotent.
end note
@enduml
